</td><td align="center">0.77 (0.37 to 1.63)</td><td align="center">0.5</td><td align="center">0.79 (0.36 to 1.72)</td><td align="center">0.5</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Haematological/oncological/transplant</td><td align="center">1.04 (0.41 to 2.60)</td><td align="center">0.9</td><td align="center">0.96 (0.35 to 2.63)</td><td align="center">0.9</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Other</td><td align="center">1.02 (0.50 to 20.7)</td><td align="center">0.9</td><td align="center">0.60 (0.29 to 1.26)</td><td align="center">0.2</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Polytrauma</td><td align="center">1.03 (0.43 to 2.49)</td><td align="center">0.9</td><td align="center">0.75 (0.29 to 1.90)</td><td align="center">0.5</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Respiratory/thoracic</td><td align="center">1.43 (0.75 to 2.71)</td><td align="center">0.3</td><td align="center">0.85 (0.44 to 1.64)</td><td align="center">0.6</td></tr><tr><td align="left">On admission blood glucose</td><td align="center">0.99 (0.99 to 1.001)</td><td align="center">0.1</td><td align="center">0.99 (0.99 to 1.002)</td><td align="center">0.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Gender, female</td><td align="center">0.68 (0.47 to 1.000)</td><td align="center"><bold>0.05</bold></td><td align="center">0.63 (0.43 to 0.93)</td><td align="center"><bold>0.02</bold></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="5"><bold>                              <italic>C. Corrected for baseline risk factors and known risk factors occurring during ICU stay.</italic>                           </bold></td></tr><tr><td colspan="5"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Glycaemic control, IIT</td><td align="center">0.25 (0.14 to 0.43)</td><td align="center"><bold>&#x0003c; 0.0001</bold></td><td align="center">0.40 (0.22 to 0.72)</td><td align="center"><bold>0.002</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left">ICU type, medical</td><td align="center">0.62 (0.33 to 1.16)</td><td align="cen